/-!
# M14 zero-capacity causal non-identifiability

The same visible actionable-exit capacity `0` is generated by three exact,
constructively different source geometries at every finite temporal depth:

* full price capture while payment, route, and actual service remain present;
* no capture and a missing payment incidence while route/service remain;
* no capture and a missing route incidence while payment/service remain.

The capacity readout therefore has a fibre with three distinct causal
origins and admits no left-inverse causal reconstruction.  This is a fixed
UBI identification no-go, not a universal claim about all empirical methods.
No second capacity algorithm, matching, ledger, service registry, or causal
oracle is introduced.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace ProcessGame
namespace Society
namespace M14ZeroCapacityCausalNonidentifiabilityRegression

noncomputable section

